  "description": "Explains the composite factor of 3 in the j=2 head criterion of habiro_head_divisibility_probe.py. A = P(-1) is an identity (the Pochhammer kills every m>=2 term at u=-1), and u=-1 is q=1, so A = denom(-1) * tr_M(q=1). The trace at q=1 is 2^(1-2A), a pure power of two, so the 3 is not in the trace: it enters through denom(-1), and traces to the literal /3 in delta = flavor_split_leading(q) = hbar_q^2 h_q [2]_q / 3, used by exactly one interface kind (averaged_weighted), which occurs exactly once per MIXED atom — the single p-n junction — and never for a pure one. Hence the closed form A(Z,N) = 2^(3Z+N) * 12^[mixed], verified on every (Z,N) with Z+N <= 6, and hence 3 is the ONLY odd prime that can ever divide A. Raising the index closes p=3 at j=3. p=2 does not close, and cannot: in Z[i] the divisor's valuation at (1-i) is capped at 4 by (i;i)_4 = 0 while four of the five atoms carry a head of valuation >= 4. All arithmetic is exact; no floating point is used anywhere in this script.",
